15
00:00:36,919 --> 00:00:39,616
and thereafter we add the type we wanna use.

16
00:00:41,093 --> 00:00:43,806
Now TypeScript knows a bunch of core types

17
00:00:43,806 --> 00:00:46,230
which are simply built into TypeScript. For

18
00:00:46,230 --> 00:00:47,835
example, the number type,

19
00:00:48,462 --> 00:00:50,420
integer numbers, but also floating point

20
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:52,555
numbers, also negative numbers. Of course,

21
00:00:52,957 --> 00:00:54,755
these are numbers, and for those we have the

22
00:00:54,755 --> 00:00:55,397
number type.

23
00:00:56,248 --> 00:00:58,561
We have the string type if we want some text

24
00:00:58,753 --> 00:01:01,403
with single or double quotes, or also with

25
00:01:01,403 --> 00:01:03,074
the template literal syntax with the

26
00:01:03,154 --> 00:01:03,668
backticks.

27
00:01:05,033 --> 00:01:06,912
Sometimes we want true or false, and for

28
00:01:06,944 --> 00:01:09,193
that we got the boolean type. The boolean

29
00:01:09,193 --> 00:01:12,277
type accepts just these 2 values, true or

30
00:01:12,325 --> 00:01:12,694
false.

31
00:01:13,690 --> 00:01:15,971
We also can define object types

32
00:01:16,677 --> 00:01:19,392
to accept an object like this, for example.

33
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:22,491
We there then also have the choice between

34
00:01:22,507 --> 00:01:25,318
