35
00:01:25,334 --> 00:01:27,968
want to specifically describe how the object

36
00:01:27,968 --> 00:01:29,911
should look like, which properties it should

37
00:01:29,911 --> 00:01:30,602
have and which

38
00:01:31,196 --> 00:01:33,091
types those properties should then have.

39
00:01:33,990 --> 00:01:36,464
We can accept array types, for example, an

40
00:01:36,512 --> 00:01:37,347
array of numbers.

41
00:01:38,182 --> 00:01:40,800
There we also can define if any content is

42
00:01:40,896 --> 00:01:43,096
allowed or if it, for example, must be

43
00:01:43,096 --> 00:01:43,530
numbers.

44
00:01:44,686 --> 00:01:46,405
And we got a bunch of other types as well.

45
00:01:46,935 --> 00:01:49,038
But let's stick to those basic types here.

46
00:01:49,745 --> 00:01:51,752
And here we clearly want a number. So we

47
00:01:51,817 --> 00:01:53,711
just add Number here

48
00:01:54,546 --> 00:01:55,237
after num1

49
00:01:55,847 --> 00:01:58,496
and after num2, it's the same, colon Number.

50
00:01:59,219 --> 00:02:00,760
And now something interesting happens.

51
00:02:01,306 --> 00:02:03,586
My IDE already complains here.

52
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:06,814
It basically tells me that the argument of

53
00:02:06,846 --> 00:02:08,419
type 1 as a string

54
00:02:09,029 --> 00:02:11,598
is not assignable to a parameter of type

55
00:02:11,598 --> 00:02:14,087
Number because a string is not a number.

56
00:02:15,018 --> 00:02:16,528
If I compile this code,

57
00:02:17,619 --> 00:02:19,160
I also get this error here.

58
00:02:19,851 --> 00:02:22,194
You see, I get the error that, well, the

59
00:02:22,194 --> 00:02:23,575
same error as before.

60
00:02:24,426 --> 00:02:27,074
Nonetheless, it did compile the code. You

61
00:02:27,074 --> 00:02:29,867
can also configure TypeScript to not compile

62
00:02:29,964 --> 00:02:32,387
if it has such an error. The default is that

63
00:02:32,387 --> 00:02:33,206
it does compile.

64
00:02:33,896 --> 00:02:35,807
And here that's good because that actually

65
00:02:35,887 --> 00:02:38,086
gives us another piece of important

66
00:02:38,086 --> 00:02:38,712
information.

67
00:02:39,755 --> 00:02:42,693
In the compiled JavaScript code, that colon

68
00:02:42,870 --> 00:02:44,459
number thing here is gone.

69
00:02:45,212 --> 00:02:47,953
Because as I mentioned before, it's a pure

70
00:02:48,113 --> 00:02:50,790
TypeScript feature. It doesn't exist in

71
00:02:50,806 --> 00:02:53,034
JavaScript. It's only there during

72
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:56,448
development to give us exactly that error

73
00:02:56,913 --> 00:02:59,445
which we see down there. That's why we have

74
00:02:59,493 --> 00:03:01,833
this feature. We only need it during

75
00:03:01,881 --> 00:03:04,414
development because it allows us to catch

76
00:03:04,446 --> 00:03:05,071
bugs like this

77
00:03:05,952 --> 00:03:07,219
and get rid of such lines.

78
00:03:08,228 --> 00:03:10,536
Now that's TypeScript in a nutshell, and

79
00:03:10,536 --> 00:03:13,341
this might sound trivial, but that's its

80
00:03:13,727 --> 00:03:16,847
core feature, the essence of TypeScript is

81
00:03:17,281 --> 00:03:19,742
that you are very clear about the types of

82
00:03:19,774 --> 00:03:21,721
data you work with in different parts of

83
00:03:21,769 --> 00:03:24,841
